  "atomic_questions": [
    "does \"exactly one student on duty for every hour\" mean that at each hour exactly one student is working (so the 14 hours are split among different students, each within their daily cap), or does it mean exactly one student is designated \"on duty\" for the entire day (which would be infeasible given the caps)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response presents a single clarification request asking the user to choose between two interpretations of the coverage rule. Although it contains two options, it requires one policy decision, so it counts as one atomic question."
}

